# DEPLOY-1 finding: docker-entrypoint.sh reached a real Ubuntu server with
# CRLF line endings (git's autocrlf=true on this Windows dev machine
# converted it during `git archive`/checkout), corrupting the shebang
# (`#!/bin/sh\r`) and crashing the backend container in a boot loop
# ("exec ./docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory" — the kernel
# looking for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r"). The stored git
# blob was already LF-only; the corruption happened purely at checkout
# time and would hit any Windows-based engineer cloning this repo with
# autocrlf enabled (a common default), not just this deployment's transfer
# method. Forcing LF here makes checkout line endings deterministic
# regardless of the cloning machine's local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
